-- title:
--   Local root count one at q ∥ N, q ≠ p
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, let $p\neq 2$ be a prime with $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual representation over $k$ (a $2$-dimensional $k$-space with a monoid map from $\mathrm{Gal}(\bar{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ to its endomorphisms trivial on some finite level) that is absolutely irreducible, i.e. its base change to $\bar k$ has no proper invariant subspace. Let $S_{\min}\subseteq S$ be finite sets of primes with $p\in S_{\min}$, such that for primes $q\neq p$ one has $q\in S_{\min}$ exactly when $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$, and such that for $q\in S_{\min}$, $q\neq p$, every inertia element at $q$ acts on $\bar\rho$ with characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$. Let $N\neq 0$ have all prime divisors in $S$, with $p^2\nmid N$, with $q\mid N$ for all $q\in S_{\min}\setminus\{p\}$, with $q^2\mid N$ for primes $q\neq p$ dividing $N$ and outside $S_{\min}$, and with no prime cube dividing $N$; assume $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ is spanned over $\mathbb C$ by its forms with integral $q$-expansions. Let $\theta$ be a ring map from the Hecke algebra $\mathbb T^{S}(N)$, the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$) and the $U_q$ ($q\mid N$ prime, $q\notin S$), to $k$, such that for every such $\ell$ and every Frobenius element $\sigma$ at $\ell$ relative to a valuation subring of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ over $\ell$ one has $\mathrm{charpoly}\,\bar\rho(\sigma)=X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Fix a prime $q\neq p$ with $q\mid N$, $q^2\nmid N$, and $c\in k$. Call $x\in\bar K:=\overline{\mathrm{Frac}\,\mathcal O}$ residually $c$ if $x$ is a root of a monic $R\in\mathcal O[X]$ whose reduction is $(X-C\,c)^{\deg R}$. For a newform datum behind an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\chi$ from the local Hecke algebra $\mathbb T^{S}(N)_\theta$ (the localisation of the base change of $\mathbb T^S(N)$ to $\mathcal O$ at the prime complement of $\ker\theta$) to $\bar K$ — a level $Mg\mid N$, a newform $g$ of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_0(Mg)$ (a normalised eigenform occurring at no proper divisor level), a ring map $\chi_g$ on $\mathbb T^{\emptyset}(Mg)$ sending $T_\ell$ and $U_q$ to the corresponding $q$-coefficients of $g$, and a ring map $\iota$ on the image of $\chi_g$ agreeing with $\chi$ on the $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$ — put $a_q=\iota(U_q)$ if $q\mid Mg$ and $a_q=\iota(T_q)$ otherwise, $e=v_q(N)-v_q(Mg)$, and $P=X-a_q$ if $e=0$, and $P=X^{e-1}\bigl(X^2-a_qX+[q\nmid Mg]\,q\bigr)$ otherwise. Assume given $\chi_0$ and $a_0\in\bar K$ residually $c$ which is a root of this $P$ for every newform datum behind $\chi_0$. The assertion is that for every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\chi$ from $\mathbb T^{S}(N)_\theta$ to $\bar K$ and every newform datum $(Mg,g,\chi_g,\iota)$ behind $\chi$, the sum of $\mathrm{rootMultiplicity}_x(P)$ over the distinct roots $x$ of $P$ that are residually $c$ equals $1$.
--
--   This is the local multiplicity-one count at a prime $q$ exactly dividing the level and distinct from $p$: once one $\bar K$-point of the local Hecke algebra has an eigenvalue residually equal to $c$ at $q$, every point contributes exactly one root residually $c$ to its local polynomial at $q$. It feeds the computation of newform multiplicities in the localised weight-$2$ Hecke algebra at a single level, [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.newformMultiplicity_finrank_iInf_eigenspace_algebraicClosure_eq_of_isCornerRealization_level_self`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.newformMultiplicity_finrank_iInf_eigenspace_algebraicClosure_eq_of_isCornerRealization_level_self).
